            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ALLIEA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent moist cake . I replaced one half of the oil with applesauce (three quarter cup applesauce three quarter cup oil and instead of just folding in lightly packed shredded zucchini I folded it in then muxed it at medium speed with my mixmaster for one to two minutes to make the batter. \r\nThen I replaced the walnuts with chocolate chips since I do not care for walnuts. Very good when frosted with the Zucchini brownie icing recipe on this site."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TRindell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very moist and yummy cake! Only used 1 cup of oil-- that was plenty. Substituted chocolate chips for the nuts. Baked in a bundt pan at 350 degrees for 50-55 minutes and dusted with confectioners sugar. Superb!!",
            "datePublished": "2006-07-28T08:10:07.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BananaPancakes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this cake for my friend's birthday party and I copied some of the changes that the other members suggested. I cut the oil to 3/4 cup and added 3/4 cup of apple sauce. And instead of using all, all-purpose flour, I used 1 cup of all-purpose and 1 cup of whole wheat. I also cut the sugar in half because the applesauce is sweet so that would make up for some of the missing sugar and then I added a tsp of vanilla. Anyway, when I brought this cake to my friends birthday party, everybody raved about it! Even my friend who hates all vegetables and fruits LOVED it (she still doesn't know that it was a zucchini cake because I haven't told her yet). AWESOME cake :)",
            "datePublished": "2007-07-15T12:44:14.660Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dahliae"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband and kids liked the cake. I will definitely bake it again. Here are my adjustments:\n\nI beat the eggs, added the sugar and sunflower oil (1 cup only). Mixed really well. Instead of cinnamon I put 1 tbsp vanilla extract.\nThen I sifted cacao and added bs, bp and salt and mixed it all well. I fine shredded the zucchini. Replaced nuts with milk chocolate chips. \nUsed regular baking, no convection - 50 mins.",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-06T01:31:01.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kitsuneluvuh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my go-to zucchini cake recipe. It's perfect for summer when my garden is overrun with zucchini. I make the recipe as written, minus walnuts due to an allergy. The cake is moist and chocolatey, with a soft and springy texture. For best results, I recommend squeezing the excess water out of the zucchini before adding and giving the resulting batter a quick mix (~ 1min) with a hand mixer on med-high to fully incorporate the ingredients into a fluffy, homogenous batter.",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-27T14:04:22.830Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "C Waite"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband has made this yummy chocolate cake recipe at least 2 or 3 times. It is moist, dense, and can easily be eaten without frosting. My husband mentioned that he uses ½ cup of unsweetened applesauce, to be able to lessen the oil to 1 Cup. He also doesn't add the cinnamon, and to my surprise(!) he doesn't squeeze out the moisture. In my opinion this is the best way to use up your monster garden zucchini. ___",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-12T04:04:20.637Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jurcovicovaz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As some other people commented, I also used 3/4 cup oil and 3/4 cup apple sauce. Also I used gluten free flour and some nuts, raisins and chopped chocolate. I got amazingly high and fluffy cake (I’m not sure if it’s because first I whipped eggs with sugar until fluffy or if that’s how it gets with this recipe, anyway that’s what I wanted). The taste is amazing, rich light and mildly sweet. Definitely I’ll keep this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2022-01-22T04:06:35.500Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dd kuhu"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made yesterday. Used Hershey’s special dark cocoa, and subbed out 1/2c oil for equal amount plain greek yogurt (so 1c oil, 1/2c yogurt). Snuck in small amount of ww pastry and almond flours, probably no more than 1/2c total. Main change was dropping sugar to 1-1/3 c as others did. Almost not sweet enough (we like less sweet desserts), since served w/ ice cream and only thin chocolate glaze from melted 63% cacao choc bar. Did fine in two round 7” diameter cake pans, toothpick testing for doneness. (Had to cut substantially domed top of one so could stack). Could go larger diameter pans if you have. Moist, held up well to stacking, and very chocolate!",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-01T21:02:47.518Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "maryann cook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made 2 changes. I used 2 t. of Delallo expresso powder, giving it a deep chocolate taste. And gluten free flour from Bella Lucia. Terrific!",
            "datePublished": "2024-08-06T17:02:34.198Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
